      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "After a trivial injury, a 16-year-old girl had pain, disability and oedema in her right arm. In a first operation the suspectedly entrapped ulnar nerve was anteposed, and in a second--because symptoms worsened--it was retroposed. The condition proved to be self-induced, by compression of the arm with a bandage."},
